Z||000000||ounmongk||05-01-2000||10:49 AM||||hey all, <BR>been saving up for a better exhaust manifold for the past few months, finally got enough money to put my dreams into motion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm looking at the new Summit catalog trying to find the Hooker brand header that will fit. I've heard something on this forum about Tri-Y headers that are available through these guys, but I can't find any in the catalog called Tri-y?! are these special order? Or am I just a mongloid? Is there anything else I should order when I go through with this? BTW, I have a 87SE (4cyl) with the dual exhaust, does that matter at all? Thanks again guys, <BR>Ohm||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||05-01-2000||03:54 PM||||The full name is Hooker Tri-Y Super Competition Header. They are great. Had them on my 87 coupe and it really opened it up! One thing is that the bottom tube comeing from the tri-y can get really close to the starter. A shield must be put on the pipe (NOT wrap!!!) to protect the starter or you go through starters every 6 months. (I had it down to 30 minute change outs.) My car was totaled before I was able to put the shield on the pipe. I was trying to put the shield on the starter without success. Contact Hooker direct!||||reg||6
